{"term":"decide","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:db339068094b515ef6","definition":"To resolve (a contest, problem, dispute, etc.); to choose, determine, or settle.","example":"The election will be decided on foreign policies.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["choose","determine","pick","elect","accept","adopt","appoint","cast","choose","crave","decide","designate","desire","determine","elect","embrace","espouse","excerpt","extract","favor","opt","pick","poll","predestine","preponderate","prefer","separate","select","settle","single out","vote","winnow"],"antonyms":["jump to conclusions","rush to judgement"],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["decidability","decidable","decidement","decide on","decide upon","decidophobia","misdecide","predecide","redecide","undecide"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d34eed31e09df8315d","definition":"To make a judgment, especially after deliberation.","example":"You must decide between good and evil.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["judge","make up one's mind"],"antonyms":["jump to conclusions","rush to judgement"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["decidability","decidable","decidement","decide on","decide upon","decidophobia","misdecide","predecide","redecide","undecide"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ec8aaf28983a5b0f5a","definition":"To cause someone to come to a decision.","example":"Your admonition decided me against my intended course of action.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["choose up","decide","determine","resolve","find","judge","posken","make a decision","make up one's mind","take a decision","work out"],"antonyms":["jump to conclusions","rush to judgement"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["decidability","decidable","decidement","decide on","decide upon","decidophobia","misdecide","predecide","redecide","undecide"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6f57986ea6b0304e55","definition":"Of a Turing machine: to return a correct answer (for some yes-or-no problem) on every possible input.","example":"No Turing Machine can decide the halting problem.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["choose up","decide","determine","resolve","find","judge","posken","make a decision","make up one's mind","take a decision","work out"],"antonyms":["jump to conclusions","rush to judgement"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["decidability","decidable","decidement","decide on","decide upon","decidophobia","misdecide","predecide","redecide","undecide"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:83cac9aa37d39efab8","definition":"To cut off; to separate.","example":"Our seat denies us traffic here; / The sea, too near, decides us from the rest.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["divorce","sever","sunder","becut","decide","discerp","disintegrate","dispart","dissever","divide","divorce","divvy up","part","partition","piecemeal","rescind","section","sever","split","split up","sunder"],"antonyms":["jump to conclusions","rush to judgement"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["decidability","decidable","decidement","decide on","decide upon","decidophobia","misdecide","predecide","redecide","undecide"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide#English","license":"CC-